{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\n    >>> largest_prime_factor(13195)\n    29\n    >>> largest_prime_factor(2048)\n    2\n    \"\"\"\n    factors = []\n    d = 2\n    temp_n = n\n\n    # Find all prime factors using trial division\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 1\n\n    # If temp_n > 1, then it's a prime factor\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n\n    # Return the largest prime factor\n    return max(factors)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if parentheses in a string are balanced using a counter-based algorithm.\n    Returns True for balanced sequences, False for unbalanced ones.\n    \"\"\"\n    balance_counter = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '(':\n            balance_counter += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            if balance_counter > 0:\n                balance_counter -= 1\n            else:\n                return False  # Premature closing bracket detected\n    return balance_counter == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string of brackets is balanced and properly ordered.\n    Uses a counter-based algorithm for O(n) time and O(1) space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    balance_counter = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '(':\n            balance_counter += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance_counter -= 1\n        # If the counter drops below zero, a closing bracket appeared prematurely or unmatched.\n        if balance_counter < 0:\n            return False\n\n    # All brackets are matched if the final counter is zero.\n    return balance_counter == 0\n```"}
