{"task_id": "HumanEval/84", "solution": "```python\ndef validate_input(N: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates if N is within the specified range [0, 10000].\n    Per critical requirements, this function assumes N is valid and does not raise errors.\n    \"\"\"\n    return True\n\ndef calculate_digit_sum(N: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all digits in the decimal representation of N.\n    It converts the number to a string to iterate through its digits efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    digit_sum_val = 0\n    if N == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    for digit_char in str(N):\n        digit_sum_val += int(digit_char)\n    return digit_sum_val\n\ndef to_binary_string(decimal: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts a decimal number to its binary string representation.\n    This uses Python's bin() function and removes the '0b' prefix.\n    \"\"\"\n    binary_repr = bin(decimal)\n    return binary_repr[2:]\n\ndef solve(N):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of digits for N and returns its binary string representation.\n    This function orchestrates input validation, digit processing, and binary conversion.\n    \"\"\"\n    # As per critical requirements, validate_input assumes valid input and does not raise exceptions.\n    _ = validate_input(N)\n\n    digit_sum = calculate_digit_sum(N)\n    binary_result = to_binary_string(digit_sum)\n\n    return binary_result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/85", "solution": "```python\ndef add(lst):\n    \"\"\"Given a non-empty list of integers lst.\n    Adds even elements that are at odd indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i, num in enumerate(lst):\n        # Check if the current index is odd (1, 3, 5, ...)\n        if i % 2 != 0:\n            # Check if the number at the odd index is even\n            if num % 2 == 0:\n                total_sum += num\n    return total_sum\n```"}
