{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting,\n    you will sort the given array in ascending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is odd,\n    or sort it in descending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is even.\n\n    Note:\n    * don't change the given array.\n\n    Examples:\n    * sort_array([]) => []\n    * sort_array([5]) => [5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5]) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5, 6]) => [6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0]\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle edge cases: empty or single-element arrays\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return array.copy()\n\n    # Calculate sum of first and last elements\n    first_last_sum = array[0] + array[-1]\n\n    # Create a copy of the array to avoid modifying the original\n    array_copy = array.copy()\n\n    # Sort based on whether sum is odd or even\n    if first_last_sum % 2 == 1:  # odd sum\n        return sorted(array_copy)\n    else:  # even sum\n        return sorted(array_copy, reverse=True)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\ndef encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Encrypts a string by shifting lowercase letters by 4 positions.\n    Non-alphabetic characters are preserved, and alphabet wraparound is handled.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 4\n    ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n    ORD_A = ord('a')\n\n    def _is_lowercase(char):\n        \"\"\"Determines if a character is a lowercase letter.\"\"\"\n        return ORD_A <= ord(char) <= ord('z')\n\n    def _wrap_around(relative_position):\n        \"\"\"Handles alphabet wraparound calculations for a given relative position.\"\"\"\n        wrapped_pos = relative_position % ALPHABET_SIZE\n        return chr(ORD_A + wrapped_pos)\n\n    def _shift_character(char):\n        \"\"\"Applies the 4-position shift to a single lowercase character.\"\"\"\n        if not _is_lowercase(char):\n            return char\n\n        current_relative_pos = ord(char) - ORD_A\n        shifted_relative_pos = current_relative_pos + SHIFT_AMOUNT\n        return _wrap_around(shifted_relative_pos)\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        result_chars.append(_shift_character(char))\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting,\n    you will sort the given array in ascending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is odd,\n    or sort it in descending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is even.\n\n    Note:\n    * don't change the given array.\n\n    Examples:\n    * sort_array([]) => []\n    * sort_array([5]) => [5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5]) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5, 6]) => [6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n\n    if len(array) == 1:\n        return array[:]\n\n    # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original array\n    array_copy = array[:]\n\n    # Calculate sum of first and last elements\n    sum_first_last = array[0] + array[-1]\n\n    # Sort ascending if sum is odd, descending if sum is even\n    if sum_first_last % 2 == 1:  # odd\n        return sorted(array_copy)\n    else:  # even\n        return sorted(array_copy, reverse=True)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "def encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Create a function encrypt that takes a string as an argument and\n    returns a string encrypted with the alphabet being rotated.\n    The alphabet should be rotated in a manner such that the letters\n    shift down by two multiplied to two places.\n    For example:\n    encrypt('hi') returns 'lm'\n    encrypt('asdfghjkl') returns 'ewhjklnop'\n    encrypt('gf') returns 'kj'\n    encrypt('et') returns 'ix'\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            shifted_pos = (ord(char) - ord('a') + 4) % 26\n            result.append(chr(ord('a') + shifted_pos))\n        else:\n            result.append(char)\n    return ''.join(result)"}
