{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\n# Helper function for prime checking as described in the Prime Checker Module.\n# It implements an efficient algorithm to determine if a number is prime.\ndef is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    # Check for divisors from 3 up to the square root of n.\n    for i in range(3, math.isqrt(n) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\n# Main function to determine if n is prime and return x or y accordingly.\n# It orchestrates prime checking and conditional value return.\ndef x_or_y(n: int, x: int, y: int) -> int:\n    if is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime using an optimized O(sqrt(n)) algorithm.\n    It efficiently handles non-positive integers and small primes as edge cases.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n <= 3:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n\ndef x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"Returns the value of x if n is a prime number, otherwise returns the value of y.\n    This function internally calls the `is_prime` helper function.\"\"\"\n    if is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    '''\n    Given a list of numbers, return the sum of squares of the numbers\n    in the list that are odd. Ignore numbers that are negative or not integers.\n\n    double_the_difference([1, 3, 2, 0]) == 1 + 9 + 0 + 0 = 10\n    double_the_difference([-1, -2, 0]) == 0\n    double_the_difference([9, -2]) == 81\n    double_the_difference([0]) == 0\n\n    If the input list is empty, return 0.\n    '''\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    result = 0\n    for num in lst:\n        # Check if number is non-negative and is an integer (including floats like 2.0)\n        if num >= 0 and num % 1 == 0:\n            # Check if number is odd\n            if num % 2 != 0:\n                result += num * num\n\n    return result\n```"}
